    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The only test class in the project is `AcceptanceTest` (the other two files are support base classes), and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `displayName` feature with logic placed where it belongs:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field in API responses.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a derived `getDisplayName()` getter (annotated `@Transient` so JPA ignores it) that returns `lastName + \", \" + firstName` from the stored names.\n\nBecause MapStruct maps by matching property names, `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto(...)` now auto-populates `displayName` from the domain model's derived getter \u2014 no mapper changes, no duplicated formatting logic, and it applies uniformly to create (`POST`) and read (`GET`) responses across both controller versions. The formatting rule lives in a single small unit on the domain object (a legitimate person-name concern) rather than being scattered into the mapper or controllers.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComputesDisplayName` \u2014 which creates an owner and asserts `$.displayName` equals `\"LastName, John\"` \u2014 passes.",
